## Rules

- **TanStack Query owns all server state.** Never store API responses in Redux.
- Every module has its own query-keys file — never share keys across modules.
- Always define `staleTime` explicitly in each query — never rely solely on the default.
- Mutations always invalidate the relevant list query on `onSuccess`.
- Hooks are always `'use client'` — never call `useQuery` / `useMutation` in a Server Component.
- Prefer `void queryClient.invalidateQueries(...)` over optimistic updates unless the UX explicitly requires it.
- Query keys for `apps/admin/`, `apps/blog/`, and `apps/web/` are independent — never share them via `packages/`.
